# Cloudflare Pages serves real static files (/assets/*, /fonts/*, favicon,
# sitemap.xml, rss.xml, robots.txt, …) and Functions (/api/*) directly — these
# rules only apply to paths with NO matching file/function.

# A missing hashed asset must return a real 404, never the SPA shell. Otherwise
# a transient miss gets served as 200 text/html and — because assets are cached
# `immutable` — that wrong-MIME HTML is pinned at the edge and white-screens the
# whole app. (This is the bug that blanked desktop.)
/assets/* /404.html 404

# SPA fallback for application routes.
/* /index.html 200
